From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felipe Paiva <felipe.paiva@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:02:37 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] shelf-order-row

General gains a Shelf Order row (Classic, Release Year) between Game
Titles and CPU, saved as `order = release-year` in Config/shelf_order.txt
the way the CPU row saves cpu.txt (ADR 0100). The new order applies at
once: the shelves are sorted again and the shelf that was selected stays
selected, its faces with it. The Settings > Screen page lists the
systems in the same order, read from the same list (ShelfOrder::platforms
through screen_row), held per thread in slot_ui::screen_page;
QuickRow::SCREEN keeps the classic order, so site (g) is unchanged.
Upstream slot-ui/tests/quick_menu.rs gains the "Shelf Order" label line
in the General labels, named site (k), approved by the maintainer on
2026-10-20.
